.TH TDE-SYSTEMD-HELPER 8 "November 2026" "tde-systemd 1.0.0" "Trinity Desktop Environment"
.SH NAME
tde-systemd-helper \- privileged helper of tde-systemd
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B pkexec
.I /opt/trinity/lib/trinity/libexec/tde-systemd-helper
.I category operation
.RI [ arguments ...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B tde-systemd-helper
carries out system changes for
.BR tde-systemd-manager (1)
and
.BR tde-journal-viewer (1).
It is not meant to be run directly. The graphical programs start it with
.BR pkexec (1),
which asks
.BR polkit (8)
for authorization. The first argument selects the polkit action, so
administrators can grant or restrict each category separately.
.PP
The helper refuses to run unless it is started as root. It accepts only
the operations listed below, validates every argument (unit names,
host names, time zones, locale names, sizes, time spans and journal
filters) and then executes the matching systemd tool directly, without a
shell and with a minimal environment.
.SH OPERATIONS
.TP
.BI "units " verb " " unit
\fIverb\fR is one of start, stop, restart, reload, try-restart,
reload-or-restart, enable, disable, reenable, mask, unmask, reset-failed
or kill. Runs \fBsystemctl\fR \fIverb\fR \fIunit\fR.
.TP
.B units daemon-reload\fR | \fBunits reset-failed
Manager wide operations.
.br
polkit action: \fBorg.trinitydesktop.tde-systemd.units\fR
.TP
.B journal rotate\fR | \fBflush\fR | \fBsync\fR | \fBverify\fR | \fBdisk-usage
.TQ
.BI "journal vacuum-size " size
.TQ
.BI "journal vacuum-time " span
.TQ
.BI "journal vacuum-files " count
Journal maintenance through \fBjournalctl\fR.
.br
polkit action: \fBorg.trinitydesktop.tde-systemd.journal\fR
.TP
.BI "journal-read " "\fR[\fP-b boot\fR] [\fP-p prio\fR] [\fP-u unit\fR] [\fP-t ident\fR] [\fP-S since\fR] [\fP-U until\fR] [\fP-g regex\fR] [\fP-n lines\fR] [\fP-k\fR] [\fP-r\fR]"
Print journal entries as JSON. Following (\fB\-f\fR) is not allowed.
.br
polkit action: \fBorg.trinitydesktop.tde-systemd.journal-read\fR
.TP
.B hostname set-hostname \fR|\fB set-pretty \fR|\fB set-icon \fR|\fB set-chassis \fR|\fB set-deployment \fR|\fB set-location \fIvalue
Change the hostname and machine information through \fBhostnamectl\fR.
.br
polkit action: \fBorg.trinitydesktop.tde-systemd.hostname\fR
.TP
.BI "timedate set-time " "\(dqYYYY-MM-DD HH:MM:SS\(dq"
.TQ
.BI "timedate set-timezone " zone
.TQ
.BR "timedate set-ntp" | set-local-rtc " \fBtrue\fR|\fBfalse\fR"
Change date and time through \fBtimedatectl\fR.
.br
polkit action: \fBorg.trinitydesktop.tde-systemd.timedate\fR
.TP
.BI "locale set-locale " VARIABLE=value ...
.TQ
.BI "locale set-keymap " keymap
.TQ
.BI "locale set-x11-keymap " "layout \fR[\fPmodel \fR[\fPvariant \fR[\fPoptions\fR]]]"
Change the system locale and keyboard through \fBlocalectl\fR.
.br
polkit action: \fBorg.trinitydesktop.tde-systemd.locale\fR
.SH EXIT STATUS
The exit status of the executed tool, or
.TP
.B 64
invalid operation or argument,
.TP
.B 77
not started as root,
.TP
.B 126, 127
the tool could not be executed (pkexec also uses these codes when
authorization fails).
.SH EXAMPLES
Allow members of the group \fBsudo\fR to manage units without a password
(\fI/etc/polkit-1/rules.d/50-tde-systemd.rules\fR):
.PP
.nf
.RS
polkit.addRule(function(action, subject) {
    if (action.id == "org.trinitydesktop.tde-systemd.units" &&
        subject.isInGroup("sudo") && subject.local && subject.active)
        return polkit.Result.YES;
});
.RE
.fi
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/share/polkit-1/actions/org.trinitydesktop.tde-systemd.policy
Definitions of the polkit actions.
.SH SEE ALSO
